In particular, the `synchronized` block only ensures that the initialization of `instance` is done atomically, but it does not ensure that the visibility of the initialization is properly propagated to other threads. This means that if a thread calls `get()` after the initialization of `instance` has completed, but before the visibility of the initialization has been propagated to that thread, the thread may still see the `instance` as `null`.

